      "text": "A central limit theorem for the characters of the infinite symmetric group and of the infinite Hecke algebra — In this paper, we review the representation theory of the inﬁnite symmetric group, and\n\n**A central limit theorem for the characters of the infinite symmetric group and of the infinite Hecke algebra**\n\n70 pp, 8 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** In this paper, we review the representation theory of the inﬁnite symmetric group, and we extend the works of Kerov and Vershik by proving that the irreducible characters of S∞always satisfy a central limit theorem. Hence, for any point of the Thoma simplex, the corresponding measures on the levels Yn of the Young graph have a property of gaussian concentration. By using the Robinson-Schensted-Knuth algorithm and the theory of Pitman operators, we relate these results to the properties of certain random per- mutations obtained by riﬄe shuﬄes, and to the behaviour of random walks conditioned to stay in a Weyl chamber.\n\n**Outline.** Front matter; 1 Representation theory of the infinite symmet; 2 Quasi-symmetric functions and a link with ra; 3 Observables of Young diagrams and their cumu; 4 Kerov-Vershik law of large numbers; 5 Central limit theorems for characters and fo; 6 Pitman operators and a link with conditioned; 7 Jones-Ocneanu traces of Hecke algebras and (",
